  "comments": [
    {
      "id": "13803",
      "body": "Hi User:600810992b411b0076aaf4cc\nplease see comments below:\n1. Given a Shopper views a line item in the cart with a quantity of 1, when they tap –, then the – button is disabled and the quantity remains at 1.\n1. Should this return a message similar to “Select Remove if you wish remove this item from your bag.”\n1. If the quantity is 1 can we make the “-” appear grey, to indicate that a client cannot complete this action\n1. Given a Shopper attempts to exceed the maximum quantity allowed per SKU or customer group, when they tap , then the  control becomes disabled, an inline error message is displayed beneath the stepper reading \"Maximum purchase quantity reached for this size\", and an error message reading \"Please correct the quantity for some products\" is displayed in the order summary panel above the Checkout CTA.\n1. Once the maximum quantity is reached the “” should be greyed out to indicate that the client cannot complete this action.\n1. If a client client proceeds to select the “” the error message for the relevant product appears but the quantity should never exceed the configured limit, as such the client will not be blocked from proceeding to complete their purchase but they are aware that they cannot increase the quantity for that product.\n1. This should not be required if the above is achievable\n1. if the client attempts to add units in excess of what is available/in stock for that variant then an error message should appear (error message copy is TBC) - but the number of units in the cart should never exceed what is available and as such the client should not be required to take corrective action and their checkout journey should not be blocked.\nAdditional dependency:\nZimmerman to confirm error messaging copy",
